**Finalizing findings and test considerations**

I'm wrapping up, noting one real finding related to test policies around mocks and race conditions during HTTP focus 
refresh. I see that tests disable focus in dev, so some issues could be missed there, but fixes for canceling 
in-flight requests and guarding fresh reads look solid. I'll highlight the reasoning behind these conclusions.
**Preparing final verdict and evidence summary**

I’m organizing the verdict with a clear medium-level finding linked to a specific source file, noting that tests 
passed without rerun and no code edits occurred after the draft. I’ll include details about read-only source review 
and how the evidence points to an old library line, arranging the findings into a neat, readable summary without extra 
