codex
Verdict: **REVISION REQUIRED.**

- **F2-1 — Medium — 
[useMeetingNoteAiMutations.ts:108](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/mutations/useMeetingNoteAiMutations.ts:108): 
an outstanding detail fetch can undo the F-2 fix.**

  **Scenario:** A background refetch reads revision 1 but its response is delayed. Another editor saves revision 2; 
processing uses revision 2, and the access check caches revision 2. The delayed revision-1 response then arrives, 
reverting the cache and falsely disabling Apply.

  **Evidence:** The revision guard checks only data already cached. 
[settleMeetingNoteCache:33](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/mutations/useMeetingNoteMutations.ts:33) writes 
without cancelling the detail fetch and excludes that query from invalidation. TanStack’s [fetch 
completion:578](E:/projects/virtual-office/node_modules/@tanstack/query-core/src/query.ts:578) subsequently writes its 
result unconditionally. The new E2E does not exercise this response ordering.

  **Fix:** Cancel the outstanding exact detail query before comparing and storing the confirmed note, preserving scope 
fencing across any await. Add E2E coverage holding a real older detail response until after the access-check refresh.

F-1’s callers preserve failure-only behavior, and its fault injection is test-only and occurs after the real RPC 
response. F-3’s whitespace check passes. Recorded passing test logs were inspected; runtime tests were not rerun.
